      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(sandbox): add skipSkillsSync config option to suppress skill sync",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nSkills are copied into the sandbox workspace on every sandbox setup. For users who do not use skills or have already deployed them through other means, this sync is unnecessary overhead.\n\nRelated: #97638\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdds skipSkillsSync as an optional boolean under agents.defaults.sandbox and agents.list[].sandbox, defaulting to false.\n\n### Key behavior changes\n\n1. **File copying skipped**: syncSkillsToWorkspace is not called when skipSkillsSync=true\n2. **Skill eligibility preserved**: computeSandboxSkillsEligibility still runs, remote skill eligibility is advertised in prompts\n3. **Safe prompt construction (P2 fix)**: When skipSkillsSync=true, the host skillsSnapshot is NOT preserved. Instead, a new snapshot is built from the snapshot's resolvedSkills with sandbox-agnostic name-only prompt entries (no host <location> paths). The skills array is preserved for env overrides.\n4. **Command/system-prompt path (P2 fix)**: When skipSkillsSync=true, the container workdir branch is skipped and the function returns empty (safe default) instead of falling through to resolveReusableWorkspaceSkillSnapshot with host paths.\n\n## User Impact\n\n```json5\n{\n  agents: { defaults: { sandbox: {\n    skipSkillsSync: true,\n    docker: { setupCommand: \"mkdir -p /workspace/skills && cp -r /preloaded-skills/* /workspace/skills/\" }\n  } } }\n}\n```\n\nSafe-use contract: Skills must be preinstalled via docker.setupCommand or docker.binds. The workspace bind-mount at /workspace shadows image-baked content, so skills baked directly at /workspace/skills/ in a custom Docker image will not survive mount. Use a separate path (e.g., /preloaded-skills/) and copy via setupCommand.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Code-level proof\n\n- resolveSandboxSkillRuntimeInputs: when skipSkillsSync=true, builds a new SkillSnapshot with name-only prompt (no <location> paths), preserves skills array for env overrides\n- commands-system-prompt.ts: !skipSkillsSync guard prevents fallthrough to host snapshot\n- computeSandboxSkillsEligibility: runs unconditionally regardless of skipSkillsSync\n- prepare.ts: passes skipSkillsSync to sandbox context\n\n### Test coverage\n\n34 tests pass (4 test files, 0 failures):\n- drops host snapshot and builds name-only prompt when skipSkillsSync is enabled\n- drops host snapshot (no remapping) when skipSkillsSync is absent (regression guard)\n- keeps snapshots for non-sandboxed runs (regression guard)\n- eligibility preserved in sandbox prompts (regression guard)\n\n### Changed files (9 files)\n\nsrc/config/types.agents-shared.ts — type definition\nsrc/config/zod-schema.agent-runtime.ts — Zod schema + safe-use contract description\nsrc/agents/sandbox/types.ts — SandboxWorkspaceInfo.skipSkillsSync\nsrc/agents/sandbox/config.ts — config resolver\nsrc/agents/sandbox/context.ts — computeSandboxSkillsEligibility + skipSkillsSync propagation\nsrc/agents/embedded-agent-runner/sandbox-skills.ts — safe name-only prompt when skipSkillsSync\nsrc/agents/embedded-agent-runner/sandbox-skills.test.ts — 2 new test cases\nsrc/agents/cli-runner/prepare.ts — pass skipSkillsSync to sandbox context\nsrc/auto-reply/reply/commands-system-prompt.ts — guard against host snapshot fallthrough\n",
        "branch": "feat/skip-skills-sync",
